WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.800
Kurds are carving out their own state called Rojava.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.400
This is Rojava, a region in
northern Syria that runs along the

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.300
border of Turkey.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.180
It's home to over a million Kurds, one of

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.240
the largest ethnic groups in the Middle
East.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.920
Until a few years ago this was a

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.920
rural and forgotten corner of Syria,
where the Kurds were denied legal status

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.340
by the Syrian government.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.400
But today, Rojava's a self governed region with a

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.100
powerful militia that led the fight
against ISIS.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.600
And it's where the Middle East's

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.840
youngest democracy is taking shape.
Surrounded by Assad's totalitarian

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.520
regime, the militant Islamic State, and a
hostile neighbor, Turkey, this is an

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.360
unlikely place for a democratic
revolution. But it was actually the

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.160
Syrian war that made Rojava
a possibility in the first place.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.180
In 2011, protests against dictator Bashar
Al-Assad erupted in Syria,

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.180
The uprising

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.500
turned into open rebellions, after he sent
his army to crack down on the opposition.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.640
With battles on multiple fronts and
forces stretched thin, he had to make a choice.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.620
By July 2012 Assad pulled most of
his army out of the traditional Kurdish

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:25.380
territories in northern Syria to defend
these major cities in the West.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:26.460
The move

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.560
created a void, but not for long.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.930
An existing Kurdish political party called

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:35.740
the Democratic Union Party stepped up to
defend and govern the region they called Rojava.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.180
They organized it into these three small

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.760
self-governed states.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.220
They set up a democratic system of local governments

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:46.350
and claimed they would to protect the
rights of all citizens, including the

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.200
multiple ethnic groups within the region.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.900
They also promoted gender equality

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.380
across all public institutions, including
their military.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.580
An all-woman military group

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.880
called the YPJ took shape and
fought alongside the Kurdish militia,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.040
called the YPG.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.400
But just as Rojava started taking shape,

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.040
it came under attack.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.600
The jihadist militia known as ISIS...

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.440
Terrorist group ISIS gaining ground...

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.960
In Syria and Iraq
right now...

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.340
In 2014, the Islamic State

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.300
swept through Syria.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:19.640
In Rojava they drove all the way to Kobanî on the

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.980
Kurdish border and laid siege to the
city.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.480
Trapped inside were thousands of

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.560
civilians and Kurdish militia fighters.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.180
As ISIS threatened to take the city,

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.900
small pockets of Kurdish fighters held
their ground until reinforcements arrived.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.420
The US provided air support
for the Kurds and together they retook Kobanî,

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.720
marking a major moment for Rojava.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.260
The Kurdish fighters proved to be one of

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.610
the most effective forces in Syria,
leading to continued US air support and

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:50.740
eventually weapons.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.980
The victory also gave
Syrian Kurds, who were denied statehood

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:59.100
for decades, an opportunity to strengthen
and expand their territory.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:04.400
With Assad still fighting in the West, the Kurds
decided to take on ISIS.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:05.959
The Kurds are

00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:09.300
the most effective fighting force
against the Islamic State...

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.460
Kurdish fighters in Syria have made significant
gains...

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.269
Killing thousands of fighters and

00:03:14.269 --> 00:03:16.140
clawing back territory...

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.960
Kurdish-led force launched an offensive today in Syria...

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.540
Pushing ISIS further and further
back...

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.220
Out of their territory in the northeastern city of Hasaka...

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.400
We are now within sight of the ISIS stronghold of Raqqa.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:31.220
As Kurdish fighters started liberating
these cities, they incorporated their

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:33.140
populations into Rojava.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.980
With the addition of multiethnic populations,

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:39.260
Rojava was renamed the Democratic
Federation of Northern Syria,

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.140
to reflect the makeup of the region.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.580
And Kurdish fighters merged with non-Kurdish

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:48.200
militias to form the Syrian Democratic
Forces, also known as the SDF.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:53.420
Western media hailed the moment as the birth of a
young democracy in the Middle East.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:58.140
And the Kurds promoted their democratic
model as a solution for a post-war Syria.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.500
But reports also claim that the Kurds
displaced non-Kurdish populations and

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.360
committed human rights abuses.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.740
In the broader region not everyone

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.140
supported the Kurdish project.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.880
On one hand the Syrian government denied its

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:15.390
existence and on the other Turkey grew
worried as Rojava expanded. See, Turkey

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:20.070
claims the Kurds in Rojava are a front
for the PKK, a Kurdish militant group

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:23.910
that's been at war with them since the
1980s and is labeled a terrorist group

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.600
by the US and the EU.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.880
So to keep Rojava from becoming a safe haven for the Kurds,

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:35.160
Turkey sent ground troops into Syria
here in August 2016, to fight both ISIS

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:39.360
and the SDF, eventually cutting off Afrin from the rest of the Federation.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:44.720
But the Kurdish offensive continued and in
late 2017 it led to the fall of ISIS in

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:45.940
its capital of Raqqa.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:49.590
The victory marked a
big win for the Kurds, but it also opened

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:50.940
up a major threat.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.340
In early 2018 Turkey
went back into Afrin and launched

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:59.580
Operation Olive Branch, a full ground
offensive against the Syrian Kurds, here.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.560
With ISIS gone, Rojava's partnerships
had weakened.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.420
In the absence of a common enemy,

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:07.220
the American motivation for
backing the Kurdish fighters has

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:11.520
declined, especially when they're up
against Turkey - a NATO ally that the US

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.220
relies on.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:15.900
Now, it's unclear how far
turkey will go to keep Syrian Kurds in check,

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.690
but without US support their
forces are under-equipped and

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.440
undermanned, against Turkey's massive
military.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.740
In this new phase of the Syrian War,

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.960
Rojava has become a vulnerable
target.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.360
And the Kurdish dream that was

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.720
created by the start of the war is
threatened by its end.

